# Copy to hostd/.env on the dedi and fill in. Never commit the filled-in copy.
# Generate the token on the dedi with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# The portal will hold the same value when it is built; until then only the runbook's checks use it.
HOSTD_API_TOKEN=

# Which host disk backups are written to. This file is the right place for it and .env.agent is not:
# compose interpolates ${HOSTD_BACKUP_DIR} in docker-compose.yml from the shell or from this file, while
# .env.agent is an env_file, which only injects variables into the running container. Setting it there
# instead leaves the bind mount silently on the default below, and backups land on the wrong disk with
# nothing complaining.
#
# Leave it unset for /srv/backups/hostd. Set it before the first `docker compose up`: moving it later
# means moving the repositories too. The container's own side of the mount stays /backups either way.
# HOSTD_BACKUP_DIR=/srv/backups/hostd
